<title>USA: USTR launches investigation on EU starch subsidies.</title>
<headline>USTR launches investigation on EU starch subsidies.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Trade Representative Charlene Barshefsky on Monday said her agency launched an investigation into allegations that European Union subsidies for modified starch were hurting U.S. producers.</p>
<p>&quot;I am very concerned about the difficulties that U.S. wheat gluten and starch producers are facing,&quot; Barshefsky said in a statement. &quot;We intend to investigate the U.S. wheat gluten industry's claim that the EU uses one of its starch subsidy programs to cut off U.S. exports of modified starch to the EU.&quot;</p>
</text>
